  "question": {
    "text": "A solenoid of length $0.5 \\mathrm{~m}$ has a radius of $1 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and is made up of ' $\\mathrm{m}$ ' number of turns. It carries a current of $5 \\mathrm{~A}$. If the magnitude of the magnetic field inside the solenoid is $6.28 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~T}$ then the value of $m$ is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "500",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mu_0 n i=B \\quad n=$ number of turns per unit length\n$\\mu_0\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\ell}\\right) \\mathrm{i}=\\mathrm{B}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{m}=\\frac{B . \\ell}{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{i}}=\\frac{6.28 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 0.5}{12.56 \\times 10^{-7} \\times 5} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~m}=500\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
